    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d2">

                <pb facs="0015" n="3" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg3"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">845C.00/5–1346: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the
                        United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-05-17T14:00:00-04:00">May 17, 1946—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4093. Telegram Rangoon<anchor n="6" xml:id="d2-f1"/> quotes highly confidential
                    source that recent instructions from London had (1) vetoed Governor’s<anchor
                        n="7" xml:id="d2-f2"/> proposal to increase powers of existing
                        Councils<anchor n="8" xml:id="d2-f3"/> prior to holding elections and (2)
                    refused consent to Aung San’s entry Executive Council due to murder charges
                    currently levied against him. Governor reported as protesting vigorously
                    London’s rulings, alleging that rigid adherence to them might well precipitate
                    open rebellion. Rangoon Version probably only part of story. Discreet inquiry
                    suggested to ascertain when new suffrage proposal for Burma is likely to be
                    considered by Parliament.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d2-f1" n="6" xml:id="d2-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram 146, May 13, 1946, noon, not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d2-f2" n="7" xml:id="d2-f2-content">
                <p>Sir Reginald Dorman-Smith.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d2-f3" n="8" xml:id="d2-f3-content">
                <p>Advisory executive and legislative councils.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
